OM ,\n559\t\n560\t pp. 1–10 .\n561\t\n562\t Cited by: § II-B .\n563\t\n564\t [24] \n565\t Q. Li et al. (2024) \n566\t\n567\t Llm-pbe: assessing data privacy in large language models .\n568\t\n569\t arXiv preprint arXiv:2408.12787 .\n570\t\n571\t Cited by: §I .\n572\t\n573\t [25] \n574\t L. Liu, J. Zhang, S. Song, and K. B. Letaief (2022) \n575\t\n576\t Hierarchical federated learning with quantization: convergence analysis and system design .\n577\t\n578\t IEEE Transactions on Wireless Communications 22 ( 1 ), pp. 2–18 .\n579\t\n580\t Cited by: § II-B .\n581\t\n582\t [26] \n583\t Z. Ma et al. (2025) \n584\t\n585\t Speech recognition meets large language model: benchmarking, models, and exploration .\n586\t\n587\t In Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence ,\n588\t\n589\t Vol. 39 , pp. 24840–24848 .\n590\t\n591\t Cited by: §I .\n592\t\n593\t [27] \n594\t Z. Ma et al. (2026) \n595\t\n596\t SLAM-llm: a modular, open-source multimodal large language model framework and best practice for speech, language, audio and music processing .\n597\t\n598\t IEEE Journal of Selected Topics in Signal Processing .\n599\t\n600\t Cited by: § III-D .\n601\t\n602\t [28] \n603\t B. McMahan et al. (2017) \n604\t\n605\t Communication-efficient learning of deep networks from decentralized data .\n606\t\n607\t In Artificial intelligence and statistics ,\n608\t\n609\t pp. 1273–1282 .\n610\t\n611\t Cited by: § III-E ,\n612\t § IV-B ,\n613\t § IV-C .\n614\t\n615\t [29] \n616\t T. Moriya, T. Ashihara, H. Sato, K. Matsuura, T. Tanaka, and R. Masumura (2023) \n617\t\n618\t Improving scheduled sampling for neural transducer-based asr .\n619\t\n620\t In Proc. of ICASSP ,\n621\t\n622\t pp. 1–5 .\n623\t\n624\t Cited by: § II-A .\n625\t\n626\t [30] \n627\t M. Nabih, D. Falavigna, and A. Brutti (2023) \n628\t\n629\t Fed-ee: federating heterogeneous asr models using early-exit architectures .\n630\t\n631\t In Proceedings of 3rd Neurips Workshop on Efficient Natural Language and Speech Processing ,\n632\t\n633\t Cited by: §I .\n634\t\n635\t [31] \n636\t T. Nguyen et al. (2023) \n637\t\n638\t Federated learning for ASR based on Wav2vec 2.0 .\n639\t\n640\t In Proc. of ICASSP ,\n641\t\n642\t pp. 1–5 .\n643\t\n644\t Cited by: § II-A .\n645\t\n646\t [32] \n647\t J. Oruh, S. Viriri, and A. Adegun (2022) \n648\t\n649\t Long short-term memory recurrent neural network for automatic speech recognition .\n650\t\n651\t IEEE Access 10 , pp. 30069–30079 .\n652\t\n653\t Cited by: § II-A .\n654\t\n655\t [33] \n656\t V. Panayotov et al. (2015) \n657\t\n658\t Librispeech: an asr corpus based on public domain audio books .\n659\t\n660\t In In Proc. of ICASSP ,\n661\t\n662\t pp. 5206–5210 .\n663\t\n664\t Cited by: § IV-A .\n665\t\n666\t [34] \n667\t J. Pfeiffer et al. (2021) \n668\t\n669\t AdapterFusion: non-destructive task composition for transfer learning .\n670\t\n671\t In EACL ,\n672\t\n673\t Cited by: § II-B .\n674\t\n675\t [35] \n676\t S. Pletenev et al. (2025) \n677\t\n678\t How much knowledge can you pack into a lora adapter without harming llm? .\n679\t\n680\t In In Proc. of NAACL ,\n681\t\n682\t pp. 4309–4322 .\n683\t\n684\t Cited by: § III-C .\n685\t\n686\t [36] \n687\t V. Pratap et al. (2020) \n688\t\n689\t Mls: a large-scale multilingual dataset for speech research .\n690\t\n691\t arXiv preprint arXiv:2012.03411 .\n692\t\n693\t Cited by: § IV-A .\n694\t\n695\t [37] \n696\t A. Radford et al. (2023) \n697\t\n698\t Robust speech recognition via large-scale weak supervision .\n699\t\n700\t In International conference on machine learning ,\n701\t\n702\t pp. 28492–28518 .\n703\t\n704\t Cited by: § III-B .\n705\t\n706\t [38] \n707\t F. Sattler et al. (2019) \n708\t\n709\t Robust and communication-efficient federated learning from non-iid data .\n710\t\n711\t IEEE transactions on neural networks and learning systems 31 ( 9 ), pp. 3400–3413 .\n712\t\n713\t Cited by: § II-B .\n714\t\n715\t [39] \n716\t S. U. Stich, J. Cordonnier, and M. Jaggi (2018) \n717\t\n71