-other as the test sets, each of which contains 10 10 10 10 hours of speech. \nWe next benchmark different chat models and find Vicuna to be a suitable LLM and fine-tuned HuBERT to be a powerful speech encoder for conducting the ASR task.\nWe pick TinyLLaMA of the 1B-magnitude and LLaMA-2 of the 7B-magnitude to make a preliminary assessment.\n TinyLLaMA \n LLaMA-2 \n TinyLLaMA-Chat \n LLaMA-2-Chat \n test-clean \n test-other \n test-clean \n test-other \n test-clean \n test-other \n test-clean \n test-other \n 16.16 \n 9.55 \n 8.97 \n 18.77 \n 7.35 \n 17.46 \n 7.03 \n 6.37 \n 6.61 \n 6.41 \n 8.94 \n 8.95 \n 6.10 \n 8.67 \n 6.37 \n 8.22 \n 7.15 \n 8.62 \n 6.79 \nAs shown in Table  3 , the Phi-2 chat model with 2.78B parameters has a comparable word error rate with LLaMA-2 with 6.74B parameters on test-other.\nVicuna is an open-source chat LLM fine-tuned on user-shared conversational data collected from ShareGPT 13 13 13 https://sharegpt.com , utilizing LLaMA as a pre-trained LLM.\nThe LLM-based ASR model shows better results when Vicuna is used as the LLM compared with LLaMA-2 and LLaMA-2-Chat.\n test-clean \n test-other \n TinyLLaMA \n 17.31M \n 8.22 \n LLaMA-2 \n 6.74B \n 7.15 \n TinyLLaMA-Chat \n 17.31M \n 8.62 \n 18.35M \n 7.19 \n LLaMA-2-Chat \n 6.74B \n 6.79 \n Vicuna \n 6.74B \n 6.47 \n Table 4: Explore the performance with different speech encoders for LLM-based ASR. The projector is fixed with linear layers and LLM is fixed with Vicuna-7B-v1.5. LS-960 means the Librispeech 960 hours dataset. \n test-clean \n test-other \n 68.95 \n 99.37 \n 7.63M \n 7.07 \n 16.01 \n 19.82M \n 87.00M \n 16.26M \n 9.50 \n 18.88M \n 6.79 \n 6.47 \n 6.35 \n HuBERT Base \n 16.26M \n WavLM Base", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "38f8b140-304d-4f8f-ac56-b2fdbafebccb", "uuid": "4215b707-cd0c-45de-aa3b-8a2e3449c133", "timestamp": "2026-07-29T09:03:13.537Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "SpeechGPT  Zhang et al. ( 2023 ) discretizes speech tokens with Hu